{
  "item": "PantElf03",
  "mu_name": "Wind Pants",
  "mu_name_from": "MuMain loads pants indexes 10 to 14 from PantElf{i+1} (ZzzOpenData.cpp line 150: `AccessModel(MODEL_PANTS + i + 10, ..., L\"PantElf\", i + 1)`), so index 12 is PantElf03, which openmu's 0.75 Armors.cs names the Wind Pants. Group 9 index 12, Player/PantElf03.bmd.",
  "why_this_one": "The Fairy Elf's third set, sold beside Silk: Elf Lala in Noria carries all five pieces at +3 (src/sim/market.cpp, kElfLala, the index-12 rows). Here so that her shelf shows the pieces it sells rather than their names.",
  "profile": "soft_armour",
  "profile_from": "Not armour, whose default is plate_steel: nothing in this set is a forged plate. The sheets are blue quilted fabric with a darker blue scroll worked into it, no metal colour anywhere but the Armor's two tan straps. See profiles/soft_armour.json.",
  "stats": {
    "note": "The item's own row, copied from OpenMU's 0.75 initialiser rather than restated, with the call it came from beside it.",
    "from": "openmu/src/Persistence/Initialization/Version075/Items/Armors.cs line 99. The 0.75 table, which is the version this server is being built to.",
    "call": "CreateArmor(12, 4, 2, 2, \"Wind Pants\", 30, 14, 32, 30, 80, 0, 0, 1)",
    "call_note": "ArmorInitializerBase.CreateArmor(number, slot, width, height, name, dropLevel, defense, durability, strengthRequirement, agilityRequirement, darkWizardClassLevel, darkKnightClassLevel, elfClassLevel). `armor.Group = (byte)(slot + 5)`, so slot 2 is group 7, 3 is 8 and 4 is 9.",
    "group": 9,
    "number": 12,
    "drop_level": 30,
    "drops_from_monsters": true,
    "slot": 4,
    "width": 2,
    "height": 2,
    "defense": 14,
    "defense_note": "Points of defence, in the row and summed into Player.ArmourDefense by Wear - see shared/Rows.cs.",
    "durability": 32,
    "requires": {
      "level": 0,
      "strength": 30,
      "agility": 80,
      "energy": 0,
      "vitality": 0
    },
    "classes": [
      "elf"
    ],
    "classes_from": "The last three ints of the call are 0, 0, 1 - the Fairy Elf alone. 80 agility beside thirty strength is the row saying the same thing in stats."
  },
  "sheets": [
    "lower_09.png",
    "lower_09b.png",
    "hide.png",
    "skin_warrior_01.png"
  ],
  "sheet_from": "Data/Player/lower_09.OZJ (128x128), lower_09b.ozt (64x64), hide.jpg and skin_warrior_01.OZJ, from MuMain. The .bmd names lower_09.jpg, lower_09b.tga, hide.jpg and skin_warrior_01.jpg; 49 of the 152 triangles are on the first, 27 on lower_09b, 14 on hide and 62 on the skin.",
  "sheet_note": "lower_09 is a pair of blue quilted hip guards with the darker scroll, laid out on a pale unused ground - mean (154, 161, 177) is mostly that ground, not the art. lower_09b is a blue fabric skirt panel with the scroll at its hem, its alpha cutting 2-3% at the edge. skin_warrior_01 is the elf's body sheet, for the bare legs; hide caps the openings.",
  "material_note": "Twenty-three islands and two answers. Islands 19 to 22 are 19, 12, 19 and 12 - skin_warrior_01's 62 exactly - in the body sheet's leg corner: her legs, skin. The other nineteen are lower_09's 49, lower_09b's 27 and hide's 14, many of them one to three triangles - the hip guards cut up by the weld, the skirt panel and the caps - and all take cloth: blue quilted fabric with the scroll painted in, nothing hard on either sheet. lower_09b's small alpha cut is the panel's ragged hem.",
